From c5db16b0dceb57d73feb90b0ef77812b17a65867 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?Ren=C3=A9=20Rebe?= <rene@exactco.de>
Date: Fri, 2 Oct 2026 22:55:05 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] draw: choose the polygon-offset mode per triangle when the
 faces differ
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

offset_first_tri() picks the fill mode - and so whether to offset - from
the first triangle's facing and then latches that decision for every later
triangle until the next flush.  With different front and back polygon
modes the latched choice is wrong for the other facing, and a zero-area
first triangle, which the clipper emits as a sliver and the cull stage
passes on with det 0, has no facing at all and selects the front mode.

Keep deciding per triangle while fill_front differs from fill_back, as the
unfilled stage already does; equal modes keep the latched fast path.

Measured on the Matrox P690 (parhelia, draw-module rasterisation):
polygon-mode-offset configs 3 and 4 (front GL_LINE, back GL_FILL) fail ->
pass; polygon-mode, polygon-offset and gl-1.4-polygon-offset unchanged.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Signed-off-by: René Rebe <rene@exactco.de>
---
 src/gallium/auxiliary/draw/draw_pipe_offset.c | 8 ++++++--
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/gallium/auxiliary/draw/draw_pipe_offset.c b/src/gallium/auxiliary/draw/draw_pipe_offset.c
index d1ad5ab..55a7d4c 100644
--- a/src/gallium/auxiliary/draw/draw_pipe_offset.c
+++ b/src/gallium/auxiliary/draw/draw_pipe_offset.c
@@ -193,8 +193,12 @@ offset_first_tri(struct draw_stage *stage,
       offset->units = 0.0f;
    }
 
-   stage->tri = offset_tri;
-   stage->tri(stage, header);
+   /* Differing front and back modes are chosen per triangle: latching the
+    * first one's decision misapplies it to the other facing, and a zero-area
+    * first triangle (a clipper sliver) has no facing at all. */
+   stage->tri = rast->fill_front == rast->fill_back ? offset_tri :
+                                                       offset_first_tri;
+   offset_tri(stage, header);
 }
 
 
